/references
.DS_Store
.venv/
__pycache__/
data/
cache/
logs/

# Every run's numbers come along: metrics.json holds the final metrics plus the full per-epoch
# history, so every table in the report can be rebuilt and reviewed without the 24 GB of audio
# or 13 h of compute behind it.
runs/*
!runs/*/
runs/*/*
!runs/*/metrics.json
!runs/*/config.json

# Weights for the runs the report quotes, so a clone can load a model rather than only read
# about one: all 18 headline runs (three arrays x K of 1 and 5 x three seeds) plus the four
# full-data detectors, 141 MB.
#
# All three seeds, not one per cell, and the reason is the headline claim itself. It is a
# statement about seed spread -- device3 at 69.3% +/- 0.7 against all24 at 70.5% +/- 1.5, a gap
# inside the noise. Seed 0 happens to be device3's best and all24's worst, so a reader who
# loaded one checkpoint per cell would measure device3 *beating* all24 and conclude something
# stronger than we are willing to claim. Shipping one seed would hand out the single misreading
# the report works hardest to prevent.
#
# Still out, 163 MB: the coherence-test arrays, the LOSO folds and the base=64 probes. Those are
# single runs whose numbers are in metrics.json and whose per-frame output is in results/preds/.
!runs/all24_K?_w32_b16_wce_s?/best.pt
!runs/device3_K?_w32_b16_wce_s?/best.pt
!runs/best6_K?_w32_b16_wce_s?/best.pt
!runs/detector_K1_w32*_s0_full/best.pt
